(6977025, 1051594, 40391, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Paul:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Abra:</b></div><hr/><i> I left you a comment during voting. I''m sure I did! (I must of stuffed up at the time). What I wanted to say is that this is such a wonderful image and I wanted to know if she (Helen hehe) was in some sort of tank?  Congrats on the TT finish. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>She was in a pool so I was wet for this one. Using a housing for my canon G11. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks for this info. I''ve been too scared to use a housing for the usual reasons. I know I will do something wrong and end up with an expensive door stop. However, to get shots anywhere near as good as this maybe worth the risk and expense.</td>', 'Originally posted by Paul: Originally posted by Abra: I left you a comment during voting. I''m sure I did! (I must of stuffed up at the time). What I wanted to say is that this is such a wonderful image and I wanted to know if she (Helen hehe) was in some sort of tank?  Congrats on the TT finish.   She was in a pool so I was wet for this one. Using a housing for my canon G11.   Thanks for this info. I''ve been too scared to use a housing for the usual reasons. I know I will do something wrong and end up with an expensive door stop. However, to get shots anywhere near as good as this maybe worth the risk and expense.', '2013-02-11 03:39:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(6980135, 1050667, 117474, '<td valign="top">A little late... but better late than never, right? <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1000203" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1000203.gif'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1000203.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1000203.gif"/></a></td>', 'A little late... but better late than never, right? ', '2013-02-16 07:38:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(6981463, 1051226, 67697, '<td valign="top">Awww, no comments for your pretty sky.  Well here it is!</td>', 'Awww, no comments for your pretty sky.  Well here it is!', '2013-02-18 23:37:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(6984896, 1051616, 30982, '<td valign="top">Ha!  Love the look - you''re being watched!  Probably a bit too much movement for those who want crisp stopped motion and not enough motion for those who like their blur, but an exceptionally good title!</td>', 'Ha!  Love the look - you''re being watched!  Probably a bit too much movement for those who want crisp stopped motion and not enough motion for those who like their blur, but an exceptionally good title!', '2013-02-23 23:31:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(6986288, 1051134, 30982, '<td valign="top">I''m not that familiar with Rothko (enough to recognize the colors) but what makes this for me is the shadow of the tree.  Where the tree has been bent by the elements, the shadow stands straight and tall.  Poignant in a way.</td>', 'I''m not that familiar with Rothko (enough to recognize the colors) but what makes this for me is the shadow of the tree.  Where the tree has been bent by the elements, the shadow stands straight and tall.  Poignant in a way.', '2013-02-26 00:23:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(7017795, 1051476, 77196, '<td valign="top">Side note - nice alliteration in the title!<br/>Look at that vote distribution - almost a perfect bell curve! No 1''s at all, but one 10. Very nice.<br/>Great subject, use of DOF. <br/>To me, the shoe is a bit too close to the bottom of the frame - a bit more carpet below the front of the shoe would help. Also, the black (strap?) behind the shoe is distracting and a bit ambiguous as to how it fits into the image. Not sure what to do with it. Having it cropped off on the right side is also quite distracting. <br/>The great thing about this image is that the distractions do not obscure the main message of the image - they are very minor. But, at the same time, attention to removing them or minimizing them would improve the image.</td>', 'Side note - nice alliteration in the title!Look at that vote distribution - almost a perfect bell curve! No 1''s at all, but one 10. Very nice.Great subject, use of DOF. To me, the shoe is a bit too close to the bottom of the frame - a bit more carpet below the front of the shoe would help. Also, the black (strap?) behind the shoe is distracting and a bit ambiguous as to how it fits into the image. Not sure what to do with it. Having it cropped off on the right side is also quite distracting. The great thing about this image is that the distractions do not obscure the main message of the image - they are very minor. But, at the same time, attention to removing them or minimizing them would improve the image.', '2013-04-10 16:39:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(7018102, 1051476, 91360, '<td valign="top">you are full of great ideas! excellent execution .<br/>the only tip i can say here, is that you need to use simple titles that free the observer''s mind..<br/> <br/>in this case maybe " high " or "Habitual"..</td>', 'you are full of great ideas! excellent execution .the only tip i can say here, is that you need to use simple titles that free the observer''s mind.. in this case maybe " high " or "Habitual"..', '2013-04-11 07:59:23.000000', NULL, 0),
